    "updated_at": "2019-12-24T01:07:19Z",
    "body": "I think one of our current priorities (at least, I see it being brought up relatively often on Discord) is to implement command mocking so that we don't have to worry about the build path. This will also make it much easier to run tests on e.g. rust-cross. Hopefully that'll be finished soon so we can stop worrying about paths to the binary at all.\r\n\r\nThis problem has been a bit of a pain for the AUR package as well (it's pretty much *the* reason I generally recommend the prebuilt binary package), so I feel your pain.",
